# nr-tui-hljs-engine: the new crate mixdog-highlight (highlight.js 10.7.3 engine + cli-highlight 2.1.11 ANSI conversion).
# Nothing here is applied by the task; the lead applies it with the wave.

[native/core/Cargo.toml]
anchor: [workspace] members = [ ... ]  (after the entry "crates/mixdog-js",)
add:    "crates/mixdog-highlight",

anchor: [workspace.dependencies] (right after the line `mixdog-js = { path = "crates/mixdog-js" }`)
add:    mixdog-highlight = { path = "crates/mixdog-highlight" }

[native/core/Cargo.lock]
anchor: between the [[package]] entries "mixdog-graph" and "mixdog-js" (alphabetical)
add (what `cargo metadata --offline` writes; no new external crate, all three dependencies are already in the lock):
    [[package]]
    name = "mixdog-highlight"
    version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = [
     "mixdog-js",
     "regress",
     "serde_json",
    ]

[native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml]
nothing: regress, serde_json and mixdog-js are used with the features other members already enable; the crate
adds the regress feature "utf16" in its own Cargo.toml (`regress = { workspace = true, features = ["utf16"] }`),
which changes no lock entry. If `cargo hakari generate --diff` reports regress (feature utf16) after the crate
joins the workspace, apply exactly what `cargo hakari generate` writes.

[native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs]
nothing: the crate registers no protocol method.

[consumers]
mixdog-markdown-ansi (task nr-tui-md-format) adds `mixdog-highlight = { workspace = true }` to its Cargo.toml and
calls `mixdog_highlight::{supports_language, highlight_ansi, HighlightTheme, SgrStyle}`.

[verify]
cargo test --offline -p mixdog-highlight
cargo test --offline -p mixdog-highlight -- --ignored live_highlight
cargo clippy --offline -p mixdog-highlight --all-targets -- -D warnings
